  <div class="slide-num">05 / 09</div>
  <div class="slide-content">
    <p class="slide-label reveal">Innovation 2</p>
    <h2 class="slide-h2 reveal">DeepSeekMoE: <em>Fine-Grained Experts</em><br>with Shared Expert Isolation</h2>
    <div class="moe-grid reveal">
      <div class="moe-card shared">
        <div class="moe-badge">Ns Shared Experts</div>
        <h4>Always Activated</h4>
        <p>Capture <strong>common knowledge</strong> across all tokens. Always active regardless of routing decisions — stable representations for universal features</p>
      </div>
      <div class="moe-card routed">
        <div class="moe-badge">Nr Routed Experts</div>
        <h4>Sparse Top-K Activation</h4>
        <p>Sparsely activated via a <strong>top-K_r router</strong>. Fine-grained segmentation increases specialization potential per expert</p>
      </div>
      <div class="moe-card routing">
        <div class="moe-badge">Device-Limited Routing</div>
        <h4>Communication Efficiency</h4>
        <p>Each token's experts are constrained to at most <strong>M devices</strong> — drastically reduces cross-node all-to-all communication overhead</p>
      </div>
      <div class="moe-card balance">
        <div class="moe-badge">Auxiliary Losses</div>
        <h4>Load Balance &amp; Token Drop</h4>
        <p>Auxiliary losses enforce <strong>balanced expert utilization</strong>. Token-dropping strategy during training prevents overflow without affecting inference</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="moe-formula reveal">
      FFN output: <span>shared experts (Ns)</span> + <span>top-Kr routed experts</span> from Nr total · Device constraint: max <span>M devices</span> per token
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

